{
  "id": "COMPOUND:40444 - PROTEIN:5943",
  "verbalization": "Sansalvamide A is consistently shown to interact with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP through multiple pathways, with the target entity MIP acting as a common intermediary in all three evidence chains. The evidence suggests that Sansalvamide A may target MIP, which in turn is a target of various compounds, all of which ultimately lead to the activation of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. This indicates a potential mechanism where Sansalvamide A influences the activity of MIP, which then modulates the function of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. The recurring involvement of MIP and the shared target relationship with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP suggest a possible role for MIP in mediating the effects of Sansalvamide A. The evidence supports a pathway where Sansalvamide A may act through MIP to regulate the activity of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, though the exact mechanism of interaction between Sansalvamide A and MIP remains to be fully elucidated.",
